ty's average high has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.19\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.12 to +0.26), about +2.5\u00b0F since 1891.","t_mon":"Lows rose in 3 of 12 months. Highs rose in 8 of 12 months.","t_rain":"Oklahoma City has gotten wetter","p_rain":"Oklahoma City's yearly precipitation has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.51 inches per decade</strong> (95% range +0.17 to +0.84), about +6.8 inches since 1891. The 1991\u20132020 normal is 36.4 inches a year. The wettest year was 2007 (56.95 in); the driest, 1901 (15.74 in).","show_snow":true,"sig_bars":{"lo":false,"hi":true},"t_year":"2026 so far: 16 daily record highs, 1 daily record low"}}